Subject: [PATCH 6/9] fix(files): reset hook state on convo change + activate
 SSE on convoId only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two frontend findings from the codex pass:

- F2 (useFileStatusStream): pathStatusByFileId and liveSessionFiles
  used to persist across conversationId / token changes when the
  FileRow stayed mounted, so chips from one conversation could bleed
  into the next (or one user into another after re-login on the same
  browser). Fix: reset both maps inside the SSE useEffect so a fresh
  connection starts from a fresh state. React bails out of no-op
  re-renders on empty-shape sets, so initial mount is free.
- F5 (FileRow): the SSE stream was gated on
  files.length > 0 || initialSessionFiles.length > 0, which prevented
  the FIRST session_file event from ever arriving for a code-
  interpreter run that produced output before any user upload —
  breaking UAT S7's live behavior. Fix: enable on Boolean(conversationId)
  alone. The early-return when both lists are empty still hides the
  empty UI; the hook itself stays alive and ready.

Tests: 4 state-reset cases (convoId×2, token, no-op) + 3 enable-
condition cases (empty files w/ convoId, empty initialSessionFiles,
no convoId at all). Existing 27 tests unchanged.
